sentences.text:
The appellant has assailed the impugned judgment on several grounds, inter alia:
(a) That sufficient opportunity for cross-examination was not granted;
(b) That there was no legally enforceable debt;
(c) That the cheque was issued as security;
(d) That complainant failed to prove financial capacity;
(e) That due to illness (paralysis), the accused could not defend the case;
(f) That contradictions in evidence were not properly appreciated.
